# UI Kit

Before adding or changing renderer UI, check `docs/ui-kit/UI-KIT.md`, `docs/ui-kit/VISUAL-SPEC.md`, and `src/renderer/components/ui`.

## Mandatory

- Use existing UI Kit primitives for generic buttons, inputs, dialogs, menus, toasts, forms, badges, cards, tabs, and overlays.
- If a reusable primitive is missing, propose `/ui-kit` before creating local UI.
- If the need is product-specific, compose local UI from UI Kit primitives.
- UI Kit components use CSS Modules, semantic tokens, Storybook, tests, and strict TypeScript.
- UI Kit components must match the visual canon in `docs/ui-kit/VISUAL-SPEC.md`.
- UI Kit components must satisfy applicable Universal Quality Gates from `docs/ui-kit/UI-KIT.md`.
- `Button` is the first visual baseline unless the user explicitly overrides the order.
- Use Radix for complex accessible behavior; do not add Tailwind or shadcn CLI output as source of truth.
- Native prop spreads must appear before internally controlled props.
- P0 UI Kit components need baseline tests and all-variant light/dark Storybook stories.
- Icon-only UI Kit components require controlled accessible labels, semantic `AppIcon`, and disabled reason tooltip coverage.
- Form controls require label/description/error wiring and invalid/disabled tests.
- Radix UI Kit components must preserve Radix focus/keyboard behavior and test open/close, escape, keyboard navigation, and controlled state where applicable.

## Forbidden

- Duplicate local button/dialog/dropdown/toast/select styles without justification.
- Product state, Use Cases, Electron, SIP, stores, repositories, or business rules inside UI Kit.
- Hardcoded product copy inside UI Kit components.
- Global component styles or hardcoded theme colors.
- CSS `filter` or `brightness` for variant hover/active states.

## Agent Flow

For reusable UI primitives, read `.cursor/skills/ui-kit-component-agent/SKILL.md` and implement one component family per session.
